// Copy this file to Config/Secrets.xcconfig (gitignored — real values never
// get committed) and fill in the values below. Leave a key out entirely if
// you don't have it yet; Debug/Release/Staging.xcconfig's REPLACE_ME
// defaults keep the app building either way, just with that provider's
// login non-functional until you add it.
//
// Where each value comes from:
//
// FACEBOOK_CLIENT_TOKEN
//   Facebook Developer Console (developers.facebook.com) → your app →
//   Settings → Advanced → Security → "Client Token". Copy it as-is.
//   (FACEBOOK_APP_ID is already real and public — set directly in
//   Debug/Release/Staging.xcconfig, not here — Facebook app IDs are meant
//   to be public-facing. Before login works you also need Settings → Basic
//   → Add Platform → iOS → Bundle ID nyc.streamr.streamr, in that same
//   console.)
//
// GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID / GOOGLE_REVERSED_CLIENT_ID
//   Google Cloud Console (console.cloud.google.com) → APIs & Services →
//   Credentials, on whatever Google Cloud project you've already created a
//   Web OAuth client in (doesn't need to be the website's own project —
//   project number 778329962048 — since the iOS app's client just needs a
//   valid consent screen somewhere, not necessarily the same one the
//   website uses) → Create Credentials → OAuth client ID →
//   Application type "iOS" → Bundle ID nyc.streamr.streamr.
//   GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID is the client ID it gives you, exactly as shown
//   (ends in .apps.googleusercontent.com).
//   GOOGLE_REVERSED_CLIENT_ID is the SAME value with the dot-separated
//   parts reversed and re-prefixed — Google's console usually shows this
//   directly too (labeled "iOS URL scheme" in the client's config page);
//   if not, take GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID's numeric prefix before the first dash
//   and rebuild it as: com.googleusercontent.apps.<that-numeric-prefix>-<the-part-after-the-dash>

// FACEBOOK_CLIENT_TOKEN = paste-here
// GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID = paste-here.apps.googleusercontent.com
// GOOGLE_REVERSED_CLIENT_ID = com.googleusercontent.apps.paste-here
